<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany sticks to Russia sanctions after Trump diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40082699e963fca54bd4f796bec91f20781360e99099c611508a3ee6cdd05550</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T09:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sticks-to-russia-sanctions-after-trump-diesel-deal/live-79627811--7157e47a4e48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sticks-to-russia-sanctions-after-trump-diesel-deal/live-79627811?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Washington announced a sanctions pause on Russian diesel, Germany has said it remains committed to pressuring Moscow and supporting Ukraine. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Demographic change: Germany's population is declining, but not everywhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0263b63a2f3e1b9d60c3233df1dfb1c30dda1969b2014a4b80679dd0916c582</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:59:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/demographic-change-germany-s-population-is-declining-but-not-everywhere/a-79615807--43b51c38e46b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/demographic-change-germany-s-population-is-declining-but-not-everywhere/a-79615807?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By 2045, Germany will have more older people, fewer workers, and a smaller population overall. Yet some regions will defy this trend. Their success depends on how much they have to offer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-11T14:58:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
